  "full_response": "Here are example `curl` commands for authenticating with different API authentication methods:\n\n---\n\n### 1. **Bearer Token (JWT/OAuth)**\n```sh\ncurl -X GET \"https://api.example.com/endpoint\" \\\n     -H \"Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9...\"\n```\n\n**Explanation:**\n- `-H` adds the `Authorization` header with the `Bearer` token.\n- Replace the token with your actual JWT or OAuth token.\n\n---\n\n### 2. **API Key (Custom Header)**\n```sh\ncurl -X GET \"https://api.example.com/endpoint\" \\\n     -H \"X-API-Key: ak_live_1234567890\"\n```\n\n**Explanation:**\n- Some APIs use a custom header (e.g., `X-API-Key`) instead of `Authorization`.\n- Replace `ak_live_1234567890` with your actual API key.\n\n---\n\n### 3. **Basic Auth (Username:Password)**\n```sh\ncurl -X GET \"https://api.example.com/endpoint\" \\\n     -u \"admin:password123\"\n```\n\n**Alternative (Base64-encoded):**\n```sh\ncurl -X GET \"https://api.example.com/endpoint\" \\\n     -H \"Authorization: Basic YWRtaW46cGFzc3dvcmQxMjM=\"\n```\n\n**Explanation:**\n- `-u` automatically encodes the credentials in Base64 and adds the `Authorization: Basic` header.\n- The alternative explicitly includes the Base64-encoded string (`admin:password123` → `YWRtaW46cGFzc3dvcmQxMjM=`).\n\n---\n\n### Bonus: **Combining Headers**\nSome APIs require multiple headers (e.g., API key + Bearer token):\n```sh\ncurl -X POST \"https://api.example.com/endpoint\" \\\n     -H \"Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9...\" \\\n     -H \"X-API-Key: ak_live_1234567890\" \\\n     -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n     -d '{\"key\": \"value\"}",
